## Live account runs

Six bundles under `proof/live-2fa/`, indexed by `proof/live-2fa/README.md`.
Four PASS, two FAIL. Both failures are kept on purpose: each recorded a real
provider finding, and both findings have regression tests
(`test_mail_parser_extracts_one_unique_code_from_html_body`,
`test_mailbox_filters_reversed_empty_uid_range`).

Totals across all six runs: 9 login requests, at most 7 verification
requests, at most 16 Govee HTTP requests, 4 delivered verification emails.
No device or MQTT endpoint was contacted in any run.

## Known gaps

The harness's own safety gates are not unit-tested: `Config.load`,
`secret_file`, `ensure_clean_worktree`, and `Probe.invoke`'s request budget.
`FakeProbe` in the test file hand-duplicates the budget check, so the real
one is never exercised. Tracked as follow-up work; stated here rather than
implied to be covered.

IMAP operations carry their own 30-second socket timeouts and do not consult
the global deadline, so a stalled server can make a run exceed the declared
10-minute bound.
